/**
\mainpage G4Cosmic Framework Overview

\section g4cosmic_purpose Purpose

G4Cosmic is a reusable Geant4 framework for cosmic-ray and particle-source
simulation studies.  It provides common application plumbing, primary-source
selection, sensitive-volume hit recording, ROOT output, and JSON run metadata.
Detector-specific meaning stays outside the framework core.

\section g4cosmic_philosophy Design philosophy

\code{.txt}
Detector code defines detector geometry and sensitive volumes.
Macros define simulation runs.
G4Cosmic provides reusable source, output, metadata, and Geant4 plumbing.
\endcode

The core records generic quantities: generated primaries, sensitive-volume
energy-deposition steps, optional track endings, reduced hit summaries, and run
provenance.  Detector-specific concepts such as bars, channels, hodoscopes,
thresholds, triggers, and labels belong in downstream detector code or analysis.

\section g4cosmic_sources Primary sources

Primary generation is selected at runtime through `/g4cosmic/source`:

\code{.txt}
/g4cosmic/source cry
/g4cosmic/source corsika
/g4cosmic/source gun
/g4cosmic/source sample
\endcode

Each source implements G4Cosmic::PrimaryGenerator and may append source-specific
metadata to the JSON sidecar.  The CORSIKA source deliberately uses an external
runner boundary, so G4Cosmic can build and run on platforms where real CORSIKA is
absent or unsupported.  A runner may launch native Linux CORSIKA, WSL, a
container, or a cluster job as long as it writes the G4Cosmic text `.dat` shower
format.

\section g4cosmic_metadata Run metadata

Every ROOT file written by the framework gets a matching JSON sidecar:

\code{.txt}
output.root
output.json
\endcode

The sidecar records runtime information, output file names, build/git metadata,
macro fingerprints and commands, source metadata, and optional detector/user
metadata supplied through append hooks.

\section g4cosmic_extension Extension points

The main extension points are:

- G4Cosmic::DetectorConstruction for downstream detector geometry.
- G4Cosmic::PrimaryGenerator for new source backends.
- G4Cosmic::JsonWriter append hooks for detector/source/user metadata.

\namespace G4Cosmic
\brief Reusable Geant4 cosmic-ray simulation framework namespace.

\details
The G4Cosmic namespace contains the public framework interfaces used by example
applications and downstream detector projects.  The namespace boundary is meant
to keep core responsibilities clear: source selection, Geant4 application setup,
sensitive-volume output, and run metadata live in the framework; detector meaning
and analysis logic live outside it.
*/
